 "findings": [
  {
   "heading": "### `across()` multiple columns",
   "segment_index": "S27.P3",
   "kind": "added",
   "en_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.qmd:604-604",
   "tr_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.vn.qmd:578-578",
   "proposition": "The Vietnamese bullet defines `num_range()` as selecting a numeric range (\"khoảng giá trị số\"); the English bullet for `num_range()` carries no description at all.",
   "reader_consequence": "A Vietnamese reader takes an unsourced definition of `num_range()` as handbook content and may select columns on that basis, where the English reader is told nothing and would consult `?num_range`.",
   "confidence": "high"
  },
  {
   "heading": "### Conditional statistics",
   "segment_index": "S23.P1",
   "kind": "untrue",
   "en_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.qmd:448-448",
   "tr_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.vn.qmd:431-431",
   "proposition": "The Vietnamese says a conditional statistic is \"số hàng tối đa đáp ứng các tiêu chí\" (the maximum NUMBER OF ROWS meeting the criteria), while the English says \"the maximum of rows that meet certain criteria\", i.e. the maximum of a value over the qualifying rows, which is what the chunk beside it computes with `max(temp[fever == \"yes\"], na.rm = T)`.",
   "reader_consequence": "A Vietnamese reader understands the section to be about counting rows that meet a condition and may reach for `sum()` or `n()` instead of the bracket-subset maximum the section actually teaches.",
   "confidence": "medium"
  },
  {
   "heading": "### Other tips",
   "segment_index": "S16.P1",
   "kind": "missing",
   "en_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.qmd:290-290",
   "tr_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.vn.qmd:280-280",
   "proposition": "The English warns \"The syntax is not simple.\" about `adorn_percentage(,,,c(cases,deaths))`; the Vietnamese bullet drops that warning and keeps only the recommendation to use `summarise()` instead.",
   "reader_consequence": "A Vietnamese reader loses the stated reason for preferring `summarise()`, so the recommendation reads as arbitrary and the reader may spend time on the unnamed fourth-argument syntax without being warned it is difficult.",
   "confidence": "medium"
  },
  {
   "heading": "### Adjustments",
   "segment_index": "S34.P3",
   "kind": "untrue",
   "en_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.qmd:885-885",
   "tr_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.vn.qmd:851-851",
   "proposition": "The Vietnamese says the n / denominator / percent display applies to \"các cột dạng danh sách\" (list-type columns), where the English says it applies to all CATEGORICAL columns, matching `all_categorical() ~ \"{n} / {N} ({p}%)\"` in the chunk below.",
   "reader_consequence": "A Vietnamese reader is pointed at a column type that does not exist in `tbl_summary()` and cannot connect the sentence to the `all_categorical()` helper in the code, so does not learn which columns the format applies to.",
   "confidence": "medium"
  },
  {
   "heading": "### Get counts",
   "segment_index": "S18.P4",
   "kind": "untrue",
   "en_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.qmd:334-334",
   "tr_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.vn.qmd:321-321",
   "proposition": "The Vietnamese says you can rename the counts column to something specific \"chẳng hạn như `name =`\" (such as `name =`), presenting `name =` as an example of the new name, where the English says you rename it by specifying the new name TO the `name = ` argument.",
   "reader_consequence": "A Vietnamese reader can read `name =` as the replacement column name rather than as the argument that carries it, and so does not learn how to rename the counts column.",
   "confidence": "medium"
  }
 ]
}